o come up with what is  going to make you different what  problems do you solve that nobody else  is done before and start pushing that  message you're going to start seeing  results I know it's hard to do something  different I know it's hard to think  outside the box I know it's how we've  been trained to do something a certain  way for years to then break that and say  I'm going to go in this new direction  but you have to do that if you try to do  what everybody else is doing you're not  going to have success you've got to  build beyond you've got to put something  unique in here so there's a couple ways  to do it the first I would look at your  past experience you've worked six years  in that industry look at your experience  in that business and try to find  something that's missing when you talk  to clients when they ask you to do  things for them what were some of the  things that your company couldn't do or  that charge too much for or that didn't  quite have the value that they need it  what were those things number 2 i'd  start going out and talking to prospects  talking to companies and just asking  them what do you need out of an event  management company what are some of the  problems you're facing just talk and  listen don't go and sell them anything  just talk to them and listen and they  will tell you things that you never  thought of then you can build into your  business that could be the hallmark of  what your whole company is built around  and number three I try to inject more of  yourself into your business what are you  staying for what do you believe in what  do you like doing what are your values  and inject that into the into the  company so for example if reliability is  your thing you know you are always  reliable you're always on time you  always get everything done as a customer  wanted ahead of schedule that's your  thing that's your mantra and you hate it  when people are not on time they don't  deliver push that let customers know yo